</section>
<section id="s19">
<h2><span class="n">19</span>Rest-Day Meal Plan (1,800 calories)</h2>
<p>Rest days trade starch for vegetables and move the shake to the afternoon. Protein stays high because muscle repair continues on rest days. Options within a meal differ by no more than about 30 calories.</p>
<h3>Breakfast, 7:00-8:00 AM</h3>
<p class="opt">Option A: Eggs and toast</p>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl meal"><colgroup><col style="width:34%"/><col style="width:26%"/><col style="width:10%"/><col style="width:10%"/><col style="width:10%"/><col style="width:10%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Food</th><th class="">Amount</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="num">Protein (g)</th><th class="num">Carbs (g)</th><th class="num">Fat (g)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Eggs, whole</td><td class="">3 large</td><td class="num">216</td><td class="num">19</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="num">14</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Ezekiel 4:9 bread</td><td class="">1 slice</td><td class="num">80</td><td class="num">5</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">0</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Berries, fresh or frozen</td><td class="">200 g</td><td class="num">90</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="num">22</td><td class="num">1</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Oil, butter, or ghee</td><td class="">5 g (1 tsp)</td><td class="num">44</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">5</td></tr><tr class="total"><td class=""><b>Meal total</b></td><td class=""></td><td class="num"><b>430</b></td><td class="num"><b>25</b></td><td class="num"><b>38</b></td><td class="num"><b>20</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="opt">Option B: Yogurt bowl</p>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl meal"><colgroup><col style="width:34%"/><col style="width:26%"/><col style="width:10%"/><col style="width:10%"/><col style="width:10%"/><col style="width:10%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Food</th><th class="">Amount</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="num">Protein (g)</th><th class="num">Carbs (g)</th><th class="num">Fat (g)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Greek yogurt, plain, nonfat</td><td class="">250 g</td><td class="num">148</td><td class="num">26</td><td class="num">9</td><td class="num">1</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Rolled oats, dry weight</td><td class="">40 g</td><td class="num">152</td><td class="num">5</td><td class="num">27</td><td class="num">3</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Berries, fresh or frozen</td><td class="">150 g</td><td class="num">68</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">0</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Peanut butter</td><td class="">10 g</td><td class="num">59</td><td class="num">2</td><td class="num">2</td><td class="num">5</td></tr><tr class="total"><td class=""><b>Meal total</b></td><td class=""></td><td class="num"><b>427</b></td><td class="num"><b>34</b></td><td class="num"><b>54</b></td><td class="num"><b>9</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Lunch, 12:00-1:00 PM</h3>
