</section>
<section id="s20">
<h2><span class="n">20</span>Food Swaps</h2>
<p>Use these when the family cooks something different or you want variety. Swap within a table, not across tables, and log what you actually ate.</p>
<h3>Protein portions (about 40 g protein each)</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl swap"><colgroup><col style="width:25%"/><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:8%"/><col style="width:23%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Food</th><th class="">Amount</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="num">Protein (g)</th><th class="num">Carbs (g)</th><th class="num">Fat (g)</th><th class="">Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Chicken breast, cooked weight</td><td class="">130 g</td><td class="num">214</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">5</td><td class="">Default. Leanest common option</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Chicken thigh, cooked weight</td><td class="">155 g</td><td class="num">324</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">17</td><td class="">Adds about 110 cal vs. breast</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Salmon, cooked weight</td><td class="">180 g</td><td class="num">371</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">22</td><td class="">Adds about 160 cal vs. breast</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Shrimp, cooked</td><td class="">165 g</td><td class="num">163</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="">Very lean</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Tuna, canned in water, drained</td><td class="">155 g</td><td class="num">180</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="">Canned in water, drained</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Ground beef 90% lean, cooked</td><td class="">155 g</td><td class="num">336</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">18</td><td class="">90% lean</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Tofu, firm</td><td class="">230 g</td><td class="num">331</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">6</td><td class="num">20</td><td class="">Firm</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Greek yogurt, plain, nonfat</td><td class="">390 g</td><td class="num">230</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">14</td><td class="num">2</td><td class="">Plain, nonfat</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Cottage cheese, 2%</td><td class="">365 g</td><td class="num">307</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">8</td><td class="">2% milkfat</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Eggs, whole</td><td class="">6 large</td><td class="num">432</td><td class="num">38</td><td class="num">2</td><td class="num">29</td><td class="">High in fat; better split across meals</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Whey protein powder</td><td class="">50 g (about 1.7 scoops)</td><td class="num">200</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">5</td><td class="num">2</td><td class="">Powder weight</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Starch portions (about 40 g carbohydrate each)</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl swap"><colgroup><col style="width:25%"/><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:8%"/><col style="width:23%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Food</th><th class="">Amount</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="num">Protein (g)</th><th class="num">Carbs (g)</th><th class="num">Fat (g)</th><th class="">Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">White rice, cooked weight</td><td class="">150 g</td><td class="num">195</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="num">42</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="">Default</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Brown rice, cooked</td><td class="">160 g</td><td class="num">197</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="num">41</td><td class="num">2</td><td class="">More fiber</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Roti, whole wheat</td><td class="">2 medium (about 80 g)</td><td class="num">240</td><td class="num">7</td><td class="num">36</td><td class="num">7</td><td class="">Varies with ghee; ask</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Potato, boiled or roasted, cooked weight</td><td class="">200 g</td><td class="num">174</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="">Most filling food tested (Section 5)</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Sweet potato, baked</td><td class="">200 g</td><td class="num">180</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="num">41</td><td class="num">0</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Rolled oats, dry weight</td><td class="">60 g</td><td class="num">227</td><td class="num">8</td><td class="num">41</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="">Dry weight</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Ezekiel 4:9 bread</td><td class="">3 slices</td><td class="num">240</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">45</td><td class="num">2</td><td class="">Also adds 15 g protein</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Lentils, cooked (plain)</td><td class="">200 g</td><td class="num">232</td><td class="num">18</td><td class="num">40</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="">Also adds 18 g protein</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Chickpeas, cooked</td><td class="">150 g</td><td class="num">246</td><td class="num">13</td><td class="num">41</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="">Also adds 13 g protein</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Fat portions (about 10 g fat each)</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl swap"><colgroup><col style="width:25%"/><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:8%"/><col style="width:23%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Food</th><th class="">Amount</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="num">Protein (g)</th><th class="num">Carbs (g)</th><th class="num">Fat (g)</th><th class="">Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Oil, butter, or ghee</td><td class="">10 g (2 tsp)</td><td class="num">88</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">10</td><td class="">Any oil, butter, or ghee</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Peanut butter</td><td class="">20 g</td><td class="num">118</td><td class="num">5</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="num">10</td><td class="">Weigh it; spoons run heavy</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Almonds</td><td class="">20 g</td><td class="num">116</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="num">4</td><td class="num">10</td><td class="">About 15 almonds</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Avocado</td><td class="">70 g</td><td class="num">112</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="num">6</td><td class="num">10</td><td class="">About one third of a medium avocado</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Fruit and vegetables</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl swap"><colgroup><col style="width:25%"/><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:9%"/><col style="width:8%"/><col style="width:23%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Food</th><th class="">Amount</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="num">Protein (g)</th><th class="num">Carbs (g)</th><th class="num">Fat (g)</th><th class="">Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Berries, fresh or frozen</td><td class="">150 g</td><td class="num">68</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="num">16</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="">Frozen is fine</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Apple</td><td class="">1 medium (about 180 g)</td><td class="num">95</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">25</td><td class="num">0</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Orange, medium</td><td class="">1 medium (about 130 g)</td><td class="num">62</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="num">15</td><td class="num">0</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Banana, medium</td><td class="">1 medium (about 120 g)</td><td class="num">105</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="num">27</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="">Fine occasionally</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Vegetables, cooked (non-starchy)</td><td class="">250 g</td><td class="num">88</td><td class="num">6</td><td class="num">18</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="">Broccoli, green beans, peppers, etc.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Salad greens, raw</td><td class="">100 g</td><td class="num">17</td><td class="num">1</td><td class="num">3</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="">Before dressing</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="note"><b>Protein bars:</b> choose bars with at least 20 g protein and no more than 220 calories. A bar can replace the afternoon snack on busy days.</p>
</section>
<section id="s21">
<h2><span class="n">21</span>Real Life</h2>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl defs"><colgroup><col style="width:28%"/><col style="width:72%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Situation</th><th class="">What to do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Family dinner is something new</td><td class="">Plate the protein first (use the protein swap table), then starch (starch swap table), then fill the rest of the plate with vegetables. Weigh and log.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Still hungry after a meal</td><td class="">Eat up to 250 g more non-starchy vegetables or salad (about 90 cal) and log them. Starting dinner with the vegetables helps (Section 5).</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Hungry late at night</td><td class="">150 g plain Greek yogurt (about 90 cal, 15 g protein), logged. If this happens 3 or more nights a week, move 75 g of dinner rice into that snack instead of adding calories.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Eating out</td><td class="">Order a protein-forward entree, ask for sauces on the side, log the closest match, and add 20% to the calories.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Holiday days (Thanksgiving, Christmas, New Year's Day)</td><td class="">Aim for about 2,500 calories. Eat the protein first at each meal, log your best estimate, and return to the plan the next day. Do not undereat the day after to make up for it.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Alcohol</td><td class="">About 150 cal per 12 oz beer, 125 per 5 oz wine, 100 per 1.5 oz shot of spirits; log it. Alcohol after training reduced muscle protein synthesis by 24% even when protein was eaten with it <sup class="cite">[<a href="#ref-61">61</a>]</sup>, and it disrupts sleep. Keep it off training nights and to 3 or fewer drinks per week.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Missed a CrossFit session</td><td class="">Eat the rest-day target that day and take the walk. Do not add a session later in the week.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Sick</td><td class="">Eat at the training-day target, keep protein at 140 g or more, sleep as much as possible, and skip training until symptoms are gone.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">One bad weigh-in</td><td class="">Ignore it. Only the seven-day average counts (Section 10).</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Office or travel day</td><td class="">Pack the snack: Greek yogurt cup, string cheese, deli turkey, a protein bar that meets the criteria in Section 20, or an apple.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>
<section id="s22">
<h2><span class="n">22</span>The Sunday Check-In</h2>
<p>Every Sunday, after the morning weigh-in, spend ten minutes on this. Record everything on the week's review page in the tracker.</p>
<ol class="steps"><li>Add up Monday through Sunday morning weights and divide by 7. That is this week's average.</li><li>Subtract it from last week's average. That is this week's change.</li><li>Check adherence: days logged (target 7), days within 100 calories of target (target 6 or more), days at 140 g protein or more (target 7).</li><li>Check recovery: average sleep hours, average energy (1 to 5), any joint pain, sessions completed.</li><li>Apply the decision table below. Change one thing at most.</li></ol>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl defs"><colgroup><col style="width:32%"/><col style="width:28%"/><col style="width:40%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">This week's change in average weight</th><th class="">Adherence</th><th class="">Action for next week</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Lost 0.5 to 1.5 lb</td><td class="">Any</td><td class="">No change.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Lost more than 1.5 lb (Week 3 onward)</td><td class="">Good</td><td class="">Add 100 cal per day: 75 g more cooked rice or 115 g more potato at dinner, every day.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Lost less than 0.5 lb, or gained</td><td class="">Not good (under 7 days logged or 2+ days off target)</td><td class="">No change to targets. Fix the logging and the off days.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Lost less than 0.5 lb, first week</td><td class="">Good</td><td class="">No change. One slow week is usually water.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Lost less than 0.5 lb, second week in a row</td><td class="">Good</td><td class="">Add 20 minutes of walking every day (about 2,000 steps). Food stays the same.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Lost less than 0.5 lb, third week in a row</td><td class="">Good</td><td class="">Cut 100 cal per day: 75 g less cooked rice or 115 g less potato at dinner, every day.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Recovery check (for the optional third hard day)</h3>
<p>From Week 9, Thursday becomes a hard day only if all four were true in the week just finished: average sleep of 7 hours or more, average energy of 3 or more out of 5, no knee or joint pain, and every scheduled session completed. If any is false, Thursday stays at RPE 7.</p>
<h3>Limits and exceptions</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl defs"><colgroup><col style="width:26%"/><col style="width:74%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Rule</th><th class="">Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Calorie floors</td><td class="">Never below 1,900 on training days or 1,600 on rest days. If you reach a floor and the trend is still flat for two weeks, take a one-week diet break at the Week 13 targets, then reassess.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Weeks 1 and 2</td><td class="">Do not add calories for fast loss. The first drop is partly water and stored carbohydrate (Section 10).</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Refeed and diet-break weeks</td><td class="">Expect the scale to rise by 1 to 3 lb from stored carbohydrate and water. Compare Week 14 with Week 12, not with Week 13.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Weeks 19 and 20</td><td class="">Follow the scheduled calorie increases and do not cut calories. Slower loss in these weeks is expected and intended.</td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Measurements</td><td class="">Waist, chest, hips, upper arm, and thigh on the Sunday of Weeks 4, 8, 12, 16, and 20. A shrinking waist with a flat scale still counts as progress.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>
<section id="s23">
<h2><span class="n">23</span>Prep Week: September 28 to October 4</h2>
<p>Use this week to set up everything so Week 1 is only about execution.</p>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl defs"><colgroup><col style="width:22%"/><col style="width:70%"/><col style="width:8%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Task</th><th class="">Details</th><th class="">Done</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Set up the app</td><td class="">Cronometer or MacroFactor. Enter 2,100 cal (training) and 1,800 cal (rest), protein target 150 g.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Stock the kitchen</td><td class="">Whey protein, creatine, eggs, Ezekiel bread, plain nonfat Greek yogurt, 2% cottage cheese, berries (frozen is fine), apples, rolled oats, peanut butter, chicken breast, rice, potatoes, vegetables.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Talk to the family</td><td class="">Ask them to set aside your chicken before sauces go on when possible, and to tell you roughly how much oil goes into each dish.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Practice weighing</td><td class="">Weigh and log every meal from Wednesday on. This is a dry run.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Baseline weight</td><td class="">Weigh in every morning Tuesday through Sunday. The average is your starting weight.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Baseline measurements</td><td class="">Sunday morning: waist at the navel, chest at the nipple line, hips at the widest point, right upper arm at mid-bicep (relaxed), right thigh at mid-thigh. Same tape, same spots, every time.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Baseline photos</td><td class="">Front, side, back. Same place, lighting, time of day, and clothing each time.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Baseline benchmarks</td><td class="">Pick three to retest in Week 18: a benchmark workout your box uses, a 3-rep max on a lift that does not bother the knee (deadlift or strict press), and max strict pull-ups or push-ups.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Talk to your coach</td><td class="">Explain the RPE plan and the knee history. Confirm the Saturday class time.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Set sleep times</td><td class="">Pick a fixed wake time and set a lights-out alarm 8 hours earlier.</td><td class=""><span class="box"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section><section class="phase" id="s24">
<h2><span class="n">24</span>Phase 1: Foundation</h2>
<p class="phase-meta">Weeks 1 to 4: October 5, 2026 to November 1, 2026</p>
<p><b>Goal:</b> Build the five-day rhythm, learn to weigh and log accurately, and establish a reliable scale trend.</p>
<h3>Week at a glance</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl glance"><colgroup><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:13%"/><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:16%"/><col style="width:11%"/><col style="width:30%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Day</th><th class="">Session</th><th class="">RPE</th><th class="">Nutrition</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="">Also</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Monday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Tuesday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Wednesday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="">30-45 min walk</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Thursday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Friday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Saturday</b></td><td class="">Week 1: Rest<br/>Weeks 2-4: CrossFit</td><td class="">Weeks 2-4: 8-9</td><td class="">Week 1: Rest day<br/>Weeks 2-4: Training day</td><td class="num">1,800<br/>2,100</td><td class="">Week 1: 30-45 min walk</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Sunday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="">Walk + check-in</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Week 1 has four sessions so the jump from two to five per week is gradual. From Week 2, Saturday is the one hard session of the week. Every other session is RPE 7 (Section 14).</p>
<h3>Daily targets this phase</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl targets"><colgroup><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:14%"/><col style="width:26%"/><col style="width:43%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Day type</th><th class="num">Calorie target</th><th class="">Protein (g)</th><th class="">Meal plan below delivers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Training day</b></td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">2,101 cal; protein 175 g, carbs 234 g, fat 54 g, fiber 32 g</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Rest day</b></td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">1,806 cal; protein 163 g, carbs 171 g, fat 54 g, fiber 31 g</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Protein must be at least 140 g every day. Calories within 100 of target on at least 6 of 7 days.</p>
<h3>Scale checkpoints</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl glance"><colgroup><col style="width:13%"/><col style="width:22%"/><col style="width:20%"/><col style="width:20%"/><col style="width:25%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Week</th><th class="">Dates</th><th class="num">Projected average (lb)</th><th class="num">On track at or below (lb)</th><th class="">Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Week 1</td><td class="">Oct 5-11</td><td class="num">185.2</td><td class="num">186.7</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Week 2</td><td class="">Oct 12-18</td><td class="num">184.4</td><td class="num">185.9</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Week 3</td><td class="">Oct 19-25</td><td class="num">183.6</td><td class="num">185.1</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Week 4</td><td class="">Oct 26 - Nov 1</td><td class="num">182.9</td><td class="num">184.4</td><td class=""></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="keep"><h3>Portions this phase</h3>
<p>Weights are cooked unless noted. Items that differ from the Section 18 and 19 base plans are highlighted. Any Option B from those sections, and any swap from Section 20, can be used instead.</p>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl spec"><colgroup><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:33%"/><col style="width:8.5%"/><col style="width:33%"/><col style="width:8.5%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Meal</th><th class="">Training day</th><th class="num">Cal</th><th class="">Rest day</th><th class="num">Cal</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Breakfast</b></td><td class="">3 eggs, 2 slices Ezekiel, 200 g berries, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">510</td><td class="">3 eggs, 1 slice Ezekiel, 200 g berries, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">430</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Lunch</b></td><td class="">120 g chicken breast, 180 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">608</td><td class="">140 g chicken breast, 100 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">537</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Afternoon (3:30-4:00 PM)</b></td><td class="">200 g cottage cheese 2%, 1 apple</td><td class="num">263</td><td class="">45 g whey + 5 g creatine, 1 apple</td><td class="num">275</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>After CrossFit</b></td><td class="">45 g whey + 5 g creatine</td><td class="num">180</td><td class="">No session</td><td class="num"></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Dinner</b></td><td class="">90 g chicken breast, 200 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">540</td><td class="">130 g chicken breast, 200 g potato, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">564</td></tr><tr class="total"><td class=""><b>Day total</b></td><td class="">P 175 g, C 234 g, F 54 g</td><td class="num"><b>2,101</b></td><td class="">P 163 g, C 171 g, F 54 g</td><td class="num"><b>1,806</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<h3>What this phase is really about</h3>
<p>Two habits: weighing and logging everything, and weighing yourself every morning. If both are automatic by the end of Week 4, the rest of the plan is straightforward. The first week's scale drop may be 1 to 3 lb, partly water and stored carbohydrate (Section 10). Do not add calories for it.</p>
<h3>Checklist</h3>
<ul class="check"><li><span class="box"></span>Weigh and log everything, every day (Weeks 1 to 3)</li><li><span class="box"></span>Morning weigh-in every day</li><li><span class="box"></span>Tell your coach about the RPE plan and your knee (start of Week 1)</li><li><span class="box"></span>Sunday check-in every week (Section 22)</li><li><span class="box"></span>Week 4 Sunday: measurements and photos</li><li><span class="box"></span>Sleep: 7.5 hours in bed, fixed wake time</li><li><span class="box"></span>Steps: 7,000 or more daily; 30 to 45 minute walk on rest days</li><li><span class="box"></span>Creatine 5 g and multivitamin daily</li></ul>
</section>
<section class="phase" id="s25">
<h2><span class="n">25</span>Phase 2: Build</h2>
<p class="phase-meta">Weeks 5 to 8: November 2, 2026 to November 29, 2026</p>
<p><b>Goal:</b> Add a second hard session and a Saturday refeed while the deficit keeps working. Thanksgiving falls in Week 8.</p>
<h3>Week at a glance</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl glance"><colgroup><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:13%"/><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:16%"/><col style="width:11%"/><col style="width:30%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Day</th><th class="">Session</th><th class="">RPE</th><th class="">Nutrition</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="">Also</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Monday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Tuesday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Wednesday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="">30-45 min walk</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Thursday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Friday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Saturday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9</td><td class="">Refeed day</td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class="">Extra carbs at lunch and dinner</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Sunday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="">Walk + check-in</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Daily targets this phase</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl targets"><colgroup><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:14%"/><col style="width:26%"/><col style="width:43%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Day type</th><th class="num">Calorie target</th><th class="">Protein (g)</th><th class="">Meal plan below delivers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Training day</b></td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">2,101 cal; protein 175 g, carbs 234 g, fat 54 g, fiber 32 g</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Rest day</b></td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">1,806 cal; protein 163 g, carbs 171 g, fat 54 g, fiber 31 g</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Saturday refeed</b></td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">2,491 cal; protein 183 g, carbs 319 g, fat 54 g, fiber 32 g</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Protein must be at least 140 g every day. Calories within 100 of target on at least 6 of 7 days.</p>
<h3>Scale checkpoints</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl glance"><colgroup><col style="width:13%"/><col style="width:22%"/><col style="width:20%"/><col style="width:20%"/><col style="width:25%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Week</th><th class="">Dates</th><th class="num">Projected average (lb)</th><th class="num">On track at or below (lb)</th><th class="">Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Week 5</td><td class="">Nov 2-8</td><td class="num">182.2</td><td class="num">183.7</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Week 6</td><td class="">Nov 9-15</td><td class="num">181.5</td><td class="num">183.0</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Week 7</td><td class="">Nov 16-22</td><td class="num">180.9</td><td class="num">182.4</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Week 8</td><td class="">Nov 23-29</td><td class="num">180.3</td><td class="num">181.8</td><td class=""></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="keep"><h3>Portions this phase</h3>
<p>Weights are cooked unless noted. Items that differ from the Section 18 and 19 base plans are highlighted. Any Option B from those sections, and any swap from Section 20, can be used instead.</p>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl spec"><colgroup><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:33%"/><col style="width:8.5%"/><col style="width:33%"/><col style="width:8.5%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Meal</th><th class="">Training day</th><th class="num">Cal</th><th class="">Rest day</th><th class="num">Cal</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Breakfast</b></td><td class="">3 eggs, 2 slices Ezekiel, 200 g berries, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">510</td><td class="">3 eggs, 1 slice Ezekiel, 200 g berries, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">430</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Lunch</b></td><td class="">120 g chicken breast, 180 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">608</td><td class="">140 g chicken breast, 100 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">537</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Afternoon (3:30-4:00 PM)</b></td><td class="">200 g cottage cheese 2%, 1 apple</td><td class="num">263</td><td class="">45 g whey + 5 g creatine, 1 apple</td><td class="num">275</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>After CrossFit</b></td><td class="">45 g whey + 5 g creatine</td><td class="num">180</td><td class="">No session</td><td class="num"></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Dinner</b></td><td class="">90 g chicken breast, 200 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">540</td><td class="">130 g chicken breast, 200 g potato, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">564</td></tr><tr class="total"><td class=""><b>Day total</b></td><td class="">P 175 g, C 234 g, F 54 g</td><td class="num"><b>2,101</b></td><td class="">P 163 g, C 171 g, F 54 g</td><td class="num"><b>1,806</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<p><b>Saturday refeed:</b> eat the training-day plan with lunch rice raised to 330 g and dinner rice raised to 350 g. That adds about 391 calories, nearly all carbohydrate, for a day total of 2,491. Protein and fat stay the same. The research on single refeed days is modest (Section 3); the main purposes here are fuel for the hardest session of the week and a planned break in hunger. It is not a free day: weigh and log as usual. Swaps: 150 g cooked rice can be replaced by 2 roti or 200 g potato (Section 20).</p>
<h3>What changes</h3>
<p>Tuesday becomes a second hard day and Saturday adds the refeed. Everything else stays the same. From Week 4 onward you may eyeball vegetables and fruit; keep weighing protein, starches, oils, and nut butters (Section 17). Expect Sunday and Monday weigh-ins to be slightly higher after the refeed; that is stored carbohydrate and water, and it evens out in the seven-day average.</p>
<p><b>Thanksgiving (Week 8, Thursday, November 26):</b> treat it as a holiday day: about 2,500 calories, protein first at each meal, back on plan Friday. If the box is closed Thursday, walk 45 minutes instead. Do not undereat on Friday to make up for it.</p>
<h3>Checklist</h3>
<ul class="check"><li><span class="box"></span>Thanksgiving (Week 8): holiday-day rule, back on plan Friday</li><li><span class="box"></span>Tuesday and Saturday at RPE 8 to 9; all others at RPE 7</li><li><span class="box"></span>Saturday refeed, weighed and logged</li><li><span class="box"></span>Sunday check-in every week</li><li><span class="box"></span>Week 8 Sunday: measurements and photos</li><li><span class="box"></span>Sleep: 7.5 hours in bed, fixed wake time</li><li><span class="box"></span>Steps: 7,000 or more daily; 30 to 45 minute walk on rest days</li><li><span class="box"></span>Creatine 5 g and multivitamin daily</li></ul>
</section>
<section class="phase" id="s26">
<h2><span class="n">26</span>Phase 3: Grind</h2>
<p class="phase-meta">Weeks 9 to 12: November 30, 2026 to December 27, 2026</p>
<p><b>Goal:</b> Hold the deficit through the point where adaptation and hunger usually build. Christmas falls in Week 12.</p>
<h3>Week at a glance</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl glance"><colgroup><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:13%"/><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:16%"/><col style="width:11%"/><col style="width:30%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Day</th><th class="">Session</th><th class="">RPE</th><th class="">Nutrition</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="">Also</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Monday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Tuesday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Wednesday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="">30-45 min walk</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Thursday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9 (see note)</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Friday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Saturday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9</td><td class="">Refeed day</td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class="">Extra carbs at lunch and dinner</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Sunday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="">Walk + check-in</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p><b>Thursday:</b> hard (RPE 8 to 9) only if last Sunday's recovery check passed: average sleep 7 hours or more, average energy 3 or more, no joint pain, every session completed. Otherwise Thursday is RPE 7.</p>
<h3>Daily targets this phase</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl targets"><colgroup><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:14%"/><col style="width:26%"/><col style="width:43%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Day type</th><th class="num">Calorie target</th><th class="">Protein (g)</th><th class="">Meal plan below delivers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Training day</b></td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">2,101 cal; protein 175 g, carbs 234 g, fat 54 g, fiber 32 g</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Rest day</b></td><td class="num">1,800</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">1,806 cal; protein 163 g, carbs 171 g, fat 54 g, fiber 31 g</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Saturday refeed</b></td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">2,491 cal; protein 183 g, carbs 319 g, fat 54 g, fiber 32 g</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Protein must be at least 140 g every day. Calories within 100 of target on at least 6 of 7 days.</p>
<h3>Scale checkpoints</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl glance"><colgroup><col style="width:13%"/><col style="width:22%"/><col style="width:20%"/><col style="width:20%"/><col style="width:25%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Week</th><th class="">Dates</th><th class="num">Projected average (lb)</th><th class="num">On track at or below (lb)</th><th class="">Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Week 9</td><td class="">Nov 30 - Dec 6</td><td class="num">179.7</td><td class="num">181.2</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Week 10</td><td class="">Dec 7-13</td><td class="num">179.1</td><td class="num">180.6</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Week 11</td><td class="">Dec 14-20</td><td class="num">178.4</td><td class="num">179.9</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class="">Week 12</td><td class="">Dec 21-27</td><td class="num">177.9</td><td class="num">179.4</td><td class=""></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="keep"><h3>Portions this phase</h3>
<p>Weights are cooked unless noted. Items that differ from the Section 18 and 19 base plans are highlighted. Any Option B from those sections, and any swap from Section 20, can be used instead.</p>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl spec"><colgroup><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:33%"/><col style="width:8.5%"/><col style="width:33%"/><col style="width:8.5%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Meal</th><th class="">Training day</th><th class="num">Cal</th><th class="">Rest day</th><th class="num">Cal</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Breakfast</b></td><td class="">3 eggs, 2 slices Ezekiel, 200 g berries, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">510</td><td class="">3 eggs, 1 slice Ezekiel, 200 g berries, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">430</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Lunch</b></td><td class="">120 g chicken breast, 180 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">608</td><td class="">140 g chicken breast, 100 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">537</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Afternoon (3:30-4:00 PM)</b></td><td class="">200 g cottage cheese 2%, 1 apple</td><td class="num">263</td><td class="">45 g whey + 5 g creatine, 1 apple</td><td class="num">275</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>After CrossFit</b></td><td class="">45 g whey + 5 g creatine</td><td class="num">180</td><td class="">No session</td><td class="num"></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Dinner</b></td><td class="">90 g chicken breast, 200 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">540</td><td class="">130 g chicken breast, 200 g potato, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">564</td></tr><tr class="total"><td class=""><b>Day total</b></td><td class="">P 175 g, C 234 g, F 54 g</td><td class="num"><b>2,101</b></td><td class="">P 163 g, C 171 g, F 54 g</td><td class="num"><b>1,806</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
