<p><b>Saturday refeed:</b> eat the training-day plan with lunch rice raised to 330 g and dinner rice raised to 350 g. That adds about 391 calories, nearly all carbohydrate, for a day total of 2,491. Protein and fat stay the same. The research on single refeed days is modest (Section 3); the main purposes here are fuel for the hardest session of the week and a planned break in hunger. It is not a free day: weigh and log as usual. Swaps: 150 g cooked rice can be replaced by 2 roti or 200 g potato (Section 20).</p>
<h3>What to expect</h3>
<p>This is where hunger and flat weeks tend to show up (Section 3). The check-in rules handle flat weeks: walk more before eating less. Use the volume strategies in Section 21 for hunger. Week 12 includes Christmas on Friday, December 25. Treat it as a holiday day: about 2,500 calories, protein first. The Saturday refeed on December 26 still happens as written. If the box is closed Friday, walk 45 minutes instead.</p>
<h3>Checklist</h3>
<ul class="check"><li><span class="box"></span>Christmas (Week 12): holiday-day rule; Saturday refeed as written</li><li><span class="box"></span>Recovery check every Sunday to decide Thursday's intensity</li><li><span class="box"></span>If the trend stalls two weeks: weigh everything for one week (Section 17)</li><li><span class="box"></span>Week 12 Sunday: measurements and photos</li><li><span class="box"></span>Sleep: 7.5 hours in bed, fixed wake time</li><li><span class="box"></span>Steps: 7,000 or more daily; 30 to 45 minute walk on rest days</li><li><span class="box"></span>Creatine 5 g and multivitamin daily</li></ul>
</section>
<section class="phase" id="s27">
<h2><span class="n">27</span>Diet Break</h2>
<p class="phase-meta">Week 13: December 28, 2026 to January 3, 2027</p>
<p><b>Goal:</b> One full week at maintenance calories over the New Year holiday to let hunger and training quality recover.</p>
<h3>Week at a glance</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl glance"><colgroup><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:13%"/><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:16%"/><col style="width:11%"/><col style="width:30%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Day</th><th class="">Session</th><th class="">RPE</th><th class="">Nutrition</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="">Also</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Monday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Tuesday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Wednesday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class="">30-45 min walk</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Thursday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Friday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class="">New Year's Day: if closed, 45 min walk</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Saturday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Sunday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class="">Walk + check-in</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Daily targets this phase</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl targets"><colgroup><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:14%"/><col style="width:26%"/><col style="width:43%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Day type</th><th class="num">Calorie target</th><th class="">Protein (g)</th><th class="">Meal plan below delivers</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Training day</b></td><td class="num">2,500</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">2,491 cal; protein 183 g, carbs 319 g, fat 54 g, fiber 32 g</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Rest day</b></td><td class="num">2,100</td><td class="">140 minimum, 150-180 target</td><td class="">2,095 cal; protein 171 g, carbs 216 g, fat 63 g, fiber 33 g</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Protein must be at least 140 g every day. Calories within 100 of target on at least 6 of 7 days.</p>
<h3>Scale checkpoints</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl glance"><colgroup><col style="width:13%"/><col style="width:22%"/><col style="width:20%"/><col style="width:20%"/><col style="width:25%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Week</th><th class="">Dates</th><th class="num">Projected average (lb)</th><th class="num">On track at or below (lb)</th><th class="">Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class="">Week 13</td><td class="">Dec 28 - Jan 3</td><td class="num">177.9</td><td class="num">179.4</td><td class="">Expect 1-3 lb higher (diet break)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="keep"><h3>Portions this phase</h3>
<p>Weights are cooked unless noted. Items that differ from the Section 18 and 19 base plans are highlighted. Any Option B from those sections, and any swap from Section 20, can be used instead.</p>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl spec"><colgroup><col style="width:17%"/><col style="width:33%"/><col style="width:8.5%"/><col style="width:33%"/><col style="width:8.5%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Meal</th><th class="">Training day</th><th class="num">Cal</th><th class="">Rest day</th><th class="num">Cal</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Breakfast</b></td><td class="">3 eggs, 2 slices Ezekiel, 200 g berries, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">510</td><td class="">3 eggs, 1 slice Ezekiel, 200 g berries, 5 g oil</td><td class="num">430</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Lunch</b></td><td class=""><span class="chg">120 g chicken breast, 330 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</span></td><td class="num">803</td><td class=""><span class="chg">140 g chicken breast, 250 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</span></td><td class="num">732</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Afternoon (3:30-4:00 PM)</b></td><td class="">200 g cottage cheese 2%, 1 apple</td><td class="num">263</td><td class=""><span class="chg">45 g whey + 5 g creatine, 1 apple, 16 g peanut butter</span></td><td class="num">369</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>After CrossFit</b></td><td class="">45 g whey + 5 g creatine</td><td class="num">180</td><td class="">No session</td><td class="num"></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Dinner</b></td><td class=""><span class="chg">90 g chicken breast, 350 g rice, 250 g vegetables, 5 g oil</span></td><td class="num">735</td><td class="">130 g chicken breast, 200 g potato, 250 g vegetables, 10 g oil</td><td class="num">564</td></tr><tr class="total"><td class=""><b>Day total</b></td><td class="">P 183 g, C 319 g, F 54 g</td><td class="num"><b>2,491</b></td><td class="">P 171 g, C 216 g, F 63 g</td><td class="num"><b>2,095</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<h3>Why a week at maintenance</h3>
<p>A planned week at maintenance lets hunger settle and training quality recover, and in the MATADOR trial dieting with maintenance breaks produced more fat loss and less metabolic slowdown than continuous dieting (Section 3). It lands on New Year's week on purpose: eating more during the holidays is part of the plan instead of a detour from it. New Year's Eve (Thursday) and New Year's Day (Friday) follow the holiday-day rule. Keep logging and weighing in.</p>
<p><b>The scale will go up.</b> Extra carbohydrate is stored with water (Section 10), so a gain of 1 to 3 lb this week is expected and is not fat. Do not make any check-in adjustment based on this week. Next week, compare the Week 14 average with Week 12.</p>
<h3>Checklist</h3>
<ul class="check"><li><span class="box"></span>Every day at the diet-break target, logged</li><li><span class="box"></span>Protein at 140 g or more every day</li><li><span class="box"></span>New Year's Eve and Day: holiday-day rule</li><li><span class="box"></span>No check-in adjustment this week</li><li><span class="box"></span>Sleep: 7.5 hours in bed, fixed wake time</li><li><span class="box"></span>Steps: 7,000 or more daily; 30 to 45 minute walk on rest days</li><li><span class="box"></span>Creatine 5 g and multivitamin daily</li></ul>
</section>
