<p><b>Saturday refeed:</b> eat the training-day plan with lunch rice raised to 330 g and dinner rice raised to 275 g. That adds about 394 calories, nearly all carbohydrate, for a day total of 2,394. Protein and fat stay the same. The research on single refeed days is modest (Section 3); the main purposes here are fuel for the hardest session of the week and a planned break in hunger. It is not a free day: weigh and log as usual. Swaps: 150 g cooked rice can be replaced by 2 roti or 200 g potato (Section 20).</p>
<h3>What changes</h3>
<p>Calories drop by 100 on every day to account for a lighter body (Section 1). The only portion change is dinner starch: 125 g of rice on training days and 75 g of potato on rest days. Training is at its hardest: Tuesday and Saturday are always hard, and Thursday is hard when the recovery check passes. Compare the Week 14 average with Week 12, because Week 13 carried extra water from the diet break.</p>
<h3>Checklist</h3>
<ul class="check"><li><span class="box"></span>Week 14: compare with Week 12, not Week 13</li><li><span class="box"></span>Scale back to the full routine: log, weigh, check in</li><li><span class="box"></span>Recovery check every Sunday</li><li><span class="box"></span>Week 16 Sunday: measurements and photos</li><li><span class="box"></span>Sleep: 7.5 hours in bed, fixed wake time</li><li><span class="box"></span>Steps: 7,000 or more daily; 30 to 45 minute walk on rest days</li><li><span class="box"></span>Creatine 5 g and multivitamin daily</li></ul>
</section>
<section class="phase" id="s29">
<h2><span class="n">29</span>Phase 5: Finish</h2>
<p class="phase-meta">Weeks 18 to 20: February 1, 2027 to February 21, 2027</p>
<p><b>Goal:</b> Peak and retest in Week 18, then deload and step calories back up toward maintenance.</p>
<h3>Week 18: peak and retest</h3>
<div class="tw"><table class="tbl glance"><colgroup><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:13%"/><col style="width:15%"/><col style="width:16%"/><col style="width:11%"/><col style="width:30%"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th class="">Day</th><th class="">Session</th><th class="">RPE</th><th class="">Nutrition</th><th class="num">Calories</th><th class="">Also</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Monday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,000</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Tuesday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,000</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Wednesday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">1,700</td><td class="">30-45 min walk</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Thursday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9 (see note)</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,000</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Friday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">7</td><td class="">Training day</td><td class="num">2,000</td><td class=""></td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Saturday</b></td><td class="">CrossFit</td><td class="">8-9</td><td class="">Refeed day</td><td class="num">2,400</td><td class="">Extra carbs at lunch and dinner</td></tr><tr class=""><td class=""><b>Sunday</b></td><td class="">Rest</td><td class=""></td><td class="">Rest day</td><td class="num">1,700</td><td class="">Walk + check-in</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Weeks 19 and 20: deload and step up</h3>
